"{\"reasoning\":\"INFEASIBLE: To meet 100\u202fMHz GBW with the 100\u202f\u00b5W power budget, the tail current must be \u226415\u202f\u00b5A, giving only ~7.5\u202f\u00b5A per input transistor. Achieving the required gm\u22483.14\u202fmS forces an impractically large W/L (~3.3\u202fk) and a sub\u20115\u202fmV over\u2011drive, and the resulting load\u2011mirror pole (\u2248100\u202fMHz) leaves insufficient phase margin. The specifications cannot be satisfied with this 5\u2011transistor OTA topology under the given power limit.\",\"W1_um\":920,\"L1_um\":0.28,\"W3_um\":200,\"L3_um\":0.5,\"W5_um\":500,\"L5_um\":0.28,\"Itail_uA\":15}"